 return dict(title='Ligand acceptance, polarization and relaxation in intact PAl12 clusters',objective='Determine how zero, one and two intact B(C6F5)3 ligands change electron attachment to the complete PAl12 core. Distinguish ligand/core localization and structural relaxation by matched neutral/anion, vertical and frozen-core controls; test whether an intact-core interpretation survives the actual endpoint and density evidence.',author='The authors hypothesize that neutral boron Lewis-acid ligation withdraws density and shifts electronic levels while retaining superatomic states, increasing electron-accepting ability independently of shell filling. The isolated aluminum-cluster source route is Gaussian 16 PBE0/def2-SVP, with binding-site and spin-multiplicity searches, same-level frequency checks and ZPE corrections. Hirshfeld charge, ESP, MO and CDA analyses use Multiwfn/VMD. PBE-D3/PAW VASP and 300-K, 10-ps AIMD are additional source stability/environment studies; they do not validate any current xTB endpoint. The complete n=0/1/2 charge-state series is source-motivated. A shared bare-neutral-core geometry, charge-matched constrained controls, explicit VEA/AEA separation and same-geometry added-electron analysis are benchmark additions. Full angular-momentum shell/CDA proof is optional in this bounded task; structural retention alone cannot establish it. Do not copy the author’s selected binding geometry or AEA values.',public={'system_specification.json':definitions,'controls.json':controls,'data_provenance.json':{'identity':'Main PDF pp2–4 and formal DOCX SI; ligand graph explicitly enumerated.','methods':'SI Computational details; original isolated molecular method recorded in PR guidance.','withheld':'No source optimized coordinates, selected attachment-site winner, orbital assignment or target AEA is public.','missing':'No validated intact ligated neutral/anion DFT pair; SI has method/figures but no full Cartesian coordinate tables.'}},remove_public=[],boundaries='Use `system_specification.json`: n0=PAl12 (13 atoms), n1=PAl12BC18F15 (47 atoms), n2=PAl12B2C36F30 (81 atoms), each at charge 0 and −1. Atoms 1–13 are the common P/Al core; ligand A uses 14–47 and B uses 48–81, with explicit covalent bonds. Neutral systems have odd electron count and even multiplicity; anions have even count and odd multiplicity. Preserve intact ligand graphs and test the complete core after every relaxation. No truncated ligand, solvent, counterion, graphene or periodic surrogate is allowed. A graph-defined initial core is not a demonstrated minimum. Full shell-orbital proof and additional ligand families are optional.',investigation='Use the staged pilot gate in `controls.json`: obtain the original intact n2 neutral/anion DFT minimum pair before expanding the full control matrix; n0/n1 are preparatory diagnostics only. For each n, explore plausible spin/site/orientation classes, optimize neutral and anion independently, validate stationary points and compare all retained candidates under a common electronic-structure convention. At each neutral minimum calculate vertical anion energy/density; separate electronic VEA, electronic AEA, ZPE-corrected AEA and anion relaxation. Freeze atoms 1–13 at a single validated neutral n0 core for the matched constrained series, relaxing only ligands; compute electronic attachment differences without borrowed thermal corrections. Analyze same-grid added-electron density and a consistent core/ligand population partition. Compare n1−n0 and n2−n1 for free, vertical and frozen-core results, and quantify basis/diffuse or state sensitivity for a decisive pair. Real, thoroughly evidenced reconstruction may exclude a candidate or invalidate an intact-model comparison; report null AEA for excluded objects, preserve coverage and do not rename an unrelated aggregate. Failure to converge once is not evidence of nonexistence. Fixed-core controls and charge analysis can bound competing explanations but cannot uniquely prove an exclusively electrostatic mechanism.',schema=result,job_schema=job,gates=['mapped_intact_models','original_n2_DFT_minimum_pair_pilot','reproducible_AEA_and_density_pilot'],guide='`results.series` has exact n0/n1/n2 entries. A `retained_pair` supplies two validated free minima, vertical anion, separate energy/ZPE quantities, fixed-core pair and density/population data. `comparisons` requires n1−n0 and n2−n1 with signed numerical differences. A complete submission requires retained n0/n1/n2 pairs and closure of the original n2 pilot. In a partial submission, a rigorously evidenced excluded n2 member may use `evidenced_exclusion`, with converged outside-identity structures, minimum/coverage evidence and null AEA; dependent comparisons must state exclusion and null differences. This records a scoped scientific falsification, never a substituted reconstructed-cluster AEA. Mere failures use partial/bounded_failure. Evidence-supported collapse of individual starting candidates is allowed when the retained endpoint coverage is complete. If the original intact n2 endpoints are absent, status remains partial/bounded_failure; missing whole panels cannot be excused as indistinguishability.',source_scope={'main.pdf':'PDF pp2–5; Fig.2 geometries, Fig.3 AEA/charge, Fig.4 orbital/CDA interpretation; Fig.5 graphene explicitly excluded.','supplementary_001.docx':'Computational details, Figs S1–S9, Table S1; checked XML text and embedded-image nature, no Cartesian list.'},source_summary='Personally read main PDF pp2–5 and visually checked Figs.2–3 on p3. The source isolated series preserves a complete P-centered Al12 shell and intact borane ligands; claims of shell retention additionally use orbital analysis. Figure 4/associated discussion distinguishes electronic-level shifts, fragment mixing and charge transfer.',si_summary='Personally read the formal DOCX SI: Gaussian16/PBE0/def2-SVP, spin/site search, same-level frequency/ZPE and Hirshfeld/Multiwfn; VASP PBE-D3 and 300-K 10-ps AIMD are separate calculations. Figs S1–S4 show optimized structures, S6–S8 electronic evidence, S9 AIMD; no complete Cartesian table is present. The original missing-SI issue is resolved, but this is not an intact-endpoint validation.',reuse='Historical run reports bounded_failure. Its raw endpoints/analysis.json shows only 3/12 or 5/12 P–Al distances below its 3.30-A diagnostic, multiple broken C–F contacts and framework_retained=false in both states. The reconstructed GFN2 aggregate value around 7.731 eV is not an AEA for the intact source cluster; nonconverged PBEh-3c attempts do not establish DFT minima. The source AEA 3.93 eV stays private and is not a tolerance or new target.',blockers=['No independently verified intact ligated neutral/anion DFT minimum pair is available despite the formal SI being present.','No common-core frozen/relaxed series, vertical attachment-density pair or calibrated n=0/1/2 uncertainty reference has been calculated.','Source drawings lack full Cartesian coordinates; independent graph-based construction and spin/site screening still require a successful pilot.'],unblock=['Build mapped n0 and n1 starts independently from complete graph/composition. Check even/odd electron parity, intact C–F/B–C connectivity and P-centered twelve-Al topology. Do not recycle reconstructed xTB endpoints as source objects.','Establish the original intact n2=PAl12[B(C6F5)3]2 neutral/anion pair using allowed DFT, unconstrained optimization, state screening and frequency/Hessian evidence. Bare-core, n1-only or forced-core success does not close the original-object gate.','Recompute AEA from separate electronic/ZPE terms and obtain same-geometry neutral/anion density plus a diffuse-basis/state sensitivity. Record costs and raw outputs; if intact endpoints cannot be established retain blocked status with bounded search evidence.','After pilot success, complete n0/n1/n2 free/fixed-core and vertical matrices, charge/density comparison and method sensitivity; calibrate numeric acceptance and independent mode trials before release.'],full_reference='Six validated free charge-state endpoints for completion; rigorously evidenced excluded n2 states can be documented in partial results, three vertical anion points, common-core electronic controls for every retained n/state, pairwise n1−n0/n2−n1 comparisons and shared-grid density/population analysis. Record candidate collapse without inventing distinct minima. Do not require full Al13/CAl12, graphene, AIMD or electrostatic embedding.',software='Allowed Gaussian/ORCA molecular engines plus supported density export/Multiwfn analysis can implement the pilot. PBE0/def2-SVP is a source baseline, not a verified diffuse-anion reference; calibrate a diffuse/basis sensitivity. xTB/CREST may generate starts but cannot substitute for intact DFT endpoints.',criteria=[('identity','Full core/ligand identity and correct charge-spin states',15,['$.results.identity_criteria','$.results.candidates','$.calculation_records','$.prerequisite_checks'],'Verify all 13/47/81-atom mapped structures, intact ligand covalent graph, complete shell and electron parity. Check unrestricted state quality and candidate coverage; formula equality alone does not preserve framework identity.'),('attachment','Free and vertical attachment energetics across ligand count',25,['$.results.series','$.results.comparisons'],'Trace neutral/anion free minima, vertical anion and state selection. Recompute AEA/VEA/ZPE and relaxation separately from logs. Never use reconstructed-aggregate AEA or swap vertical and adiabatic references. Evidenced exclusion needs actual converged reconstruction/minimum/state-coverage evidence, null invalid AEA and honest bounds.'),('core_control','Common-core frozen versus relaxed comparison',20,['$.results.series','$.results.comparisons'],'Verify identical mapped n0-neutral core coordinates in all constrained cases, actual constraints and ligand-only relaxation; inspect electronic energy differences and compare them to the free and vertical quantities. No transferred thermal correction or claim of spontaneous stability from restraint.'),('density','Added-electron localization and core/ligand population',20,['$.results.series','$.results.density_checks'],'Inspect exported neutral/vertical-anion densities on identical nuclear geometry/grid; integrate added electron number and consistent fragment charges. Check normalization and grid sensitivity, distinguish ordinary ground-state ligand charge transfer from localization of the added electron. Neither a charge scheme nor structural core retention alone proves superatomic-shell preservation or exclusive polarization.'),('discrimination','Ligand-count trends and quantitative falsification/sensitivity',10,['$.hypotheses','$.sensitivity','$.results.comparisons'],'Both n1−n0 and n2−n1 controls must be evaluated or excluded by sufficient computation. Support/refutation/ambiguity follows actual uncertainty. Missing DFT endpoints or one failed optimization do not establish absence; evidence-based collapse is acceptable.')],failures=['Substitutes a reconstructed xTB aggregate, a truncated ligand/core, or a constrained structure for a validated intact free endpoint.','Uses odd multiplicity for the odd-electron neutral or even multiplicity for its even-electron anion without correcting the actual object.','Confuses VEA, electronic AEA, ZPE-corrected AEA or constrained-core attachment; borrows thermal terms from another geometry.','Compares densities at different geometries as a pure added-electron distribution, or infers exclusive polarization/superatom shells solely from one population charge.'])

